Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?=EF=BB=BFD5=20(review):=20hand=20the=20firs?=
 =?UTF-8?q?t-round=20trigger=20to=20the=20proactive=20kernel?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LoopRuntime.verifyNow no longer starts InteractionActivity itself: a first-round Show is
submitted to the proactive kernel as an app_enter EventRequest (needsAgent=false, the
round-1 fixed sentence as its only fallback, payload limited to packageName and localTime).

The kernel then owns the arbitration: DSH busy, prompts, quiet hours, the daily cap, the
notification fallback and the presentation token. If the kernel refuses (queue full,
duplicate, feature off) the round-1 event is closed as UNAVAILABLE(kernel_<reason>) instead
of being left open with no surface that could ever appear.

Waiting for Claude: this touches the seam between the first round and the kernel, which the
integration guide marks review-before-merge. Do not merge into the candidate build yet.
