From d07bc14cbcbf4f6b1d6e9f05bcfd6152dcfbf724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:49:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix the D5 seam, the feature switches and protected
 pages; deny tools in proactive turns

Review round 3 of the proactive integration.

A. One owner per app-enter event. D5 handed the event to the kernel but never wrote the
   kernel's verdict back, so LoopEngine kept it TRIGGERED and suppressed every later visit
   with interaction_open. The kernel now owns how the event ends; LoopEngine keeps a delegated
   twin with the same eventId that KernelMirror closes exactly once (shown, every outcome,
   refusals and merges at submit, and reconcile after a restart in either start order).
   LoopEngine.recover and config changes no longer close delegated twins themselves.

B. Separate switches. The coordinator's gate used only the proactive-chat switch, so the
   trigger test was refused whenever proactive chat was off. Switches defines who runs what:
   observation and arbitration run for either feature; turning one off cancels only its own
   events (Coordinator.cancelSource), and a new test app cancels app-enter events for the old
   one.

C. Protected pages no longer depend on the trigger test. Foreground reading runs for either
   feature, is cleared when the accessibility service goes away, and the gate treats the whole
   Settings app as protected (titles are never read, so its permission pages cannot be told
   apart).

E. The host plugin denies every tool call in a turn started by a proactive message, at
   tools/pre-execute (global, prepended), until that turn ends. Verified against a real DSH
   0.2.1-rc.4 engine with a mock model that calls a tool: denied in the proactive turn, run
   normally in the person's own turn. Also fixes a startup race where an unloaded LoopEngine
   read as "trigger test off" and cancelled live events with the wrong reason.

D. tooling/verify_apk_runtime.py proves from an APK whether its rootfs carries the plugin,
   its load row and no test files; runtime/tests/test_proactive_packaging.py covers the
   rtbuild recipe.

Tests: 108 JVM (12 new), plugin 12/12, live engine 32/32, verifier 5/5, packaging 4/4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VUAnRqEK1Me9rrDHoEiwk9
